{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/fyhovuxo","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":88,"top":209.83,"width":1080.86,"height":456.83},"name":"Google Shape;98;p15","placeholder":"body","text":"Una cuerda transmite energía; su rapidez depende de la tensión y la masa por longitud.\nONDA LAB permite variar T, μ, f, A y L y observar el efecto en tiempo real.\nObjetivo: relacionar parámetros, movimiento transversal y resultados calculados.\nAlcance: simulación local, calculadora física y gráficas; sin backend.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ofy9wn61","slideIndex":2,"text":""}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/jyx0ra1s","slideIndex":3,"layout":{"id":"ly/p83mt83u","name":"OBJECT"},"title":"Modelo físico de la cuerda","textShapes":2}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/l8bad83y","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":88,"top":31.85,"width":1014.49,"height":139.17},"name":"Google Shape;103;p16","placeholder":"title","text":"Modelo físico de la cuerda","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":53.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin Medium","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ah0byt4b","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":88,"top":209.83,"width":1080.86,"height":456.83},"name":"Google Shape;104;p16","placeholder":"body","text":"Rapidez: v = √(T/μ)     Longitud de onda: λ = v/f\nFrecuencia angular: ω = 2πf     Número de onda: k = 2π/λ\nProgresiva: y(x,t) = A sin(kx − ωt)\nCuerda fija: λₙ = 2L/n     fₙ = nv/(2L)\nSupuesto: cuerda uniforme, tensión constante y pequeñas deformaciones.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/jyx0ra1s","slideIndex":3,"text":""}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/i107q5of","slideIndex":4,"layout":{"id":"ly/p83mt83u","name":"OBJECT"},"title":"Onda progresiva","textShapes":2}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/jalojqxk","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":88,"top":31.85,"width":1014.49,"height":139.17},"name":"Google Shape;109;p17","placeholder":"title","text":"Onda progresiva","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":53.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin Medium","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lorapoz2","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":88,"top":209.83,"width":1080.86,"height":456.83},"name":"Google Shape;110;p17","placeholder":"body","text":"y(x,t) = A sin(kx − ωt)\nLa fase kx − ωt avanza hacia la derecha.\nLas partículas oscilan verticalmente; no viajan junto con la onda.\nCanvas dibuja cuerda, partículas, equilibrio y sentido de propagación.\nLa rapidez se calcula con T y μ; A cambia el desplazamiento.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/i107q5of","slideIndex":4,"text":""}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/x8f69ofe","slideIndex":5,"layout":{"id":"ly/p83mt83u","name":"OBJECT"},"title":"Onda estacionaria","textShapes":2}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/7al07yd0","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":88,"top":31.85,"width":1014.49,"height":139.17},"name":"Google Shape;115;p18","placeholder":"title","text":"Onda estacionaria","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":53.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin Medium","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8buhg3ul","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":88,"top":209.83,"width":1080.86,"height":456.83},"name":"Google Shape;116;p18","placeholder":"body","text":"Los dos extremos fijos son nodos.\nEl armónico n tiene n vientres y n−1 nodos interiores.\nλₙ = 2L/n     fₙ = nv/(2L)\ny(x,t) = 2A sin(kₙx) cos(ωₙt)\nA es la amplitud de cada onda viajera; el antinodo alcanza 2A.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/x8f69ofe","slideIndex":5,"text":""}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/gnmp4jqx","slideIndex":6,"layout":{"id":"ly/p83mt83u","name":"OBJECT"},"title":"Laboratorio de parámetros","textShapes":2}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/83q5knq5","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":88,"top":31.85,"width":1014.49,"height":139.17},"name":"Google Shape;121;p19","placeholder":"title","text":"Laboratorio de parámetros","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":53.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin Medium","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/72hobi9k","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":88,"top":209.83,"width":1080.86,"height":456.83},"name":"Google Shape;122;p19","placeholder":"body","text":"Entradas: tensión T (N), densidad μ (kg/m), frecuencia f (Hz), amplitud A (m) y longitud L (m).\nResultados en vivo: v, λ, ω, k y período P.\nDeslizadores y campos numéricos están sincronizados y limitados a rangos físicos.\nEn el modelo ideal, cambiar A no altera v.\nCaso de referencia: T=50 N, μ=0.008 kg/m, f=5 Hz, L=2 m.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gnmp4jqx","slideIndex":6,"text":""}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/fu1gfa1s","slideIndex":7,"layout":{"id":"ly/p83mt83u","name":"OBJECT"},"title":"Implementación y análisis","textShapes":2}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/vi14rmdg","slideIndex":7,"position":{"left":88,"top":31.85,"width":1014.49,"height":139.17},"name":"Google Shape;127;p20","placeholder":"title","text":"Implementación y análisis","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":53.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin Medium","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8falw7e5","slideIndex":7,"position":{"left":88,"top":209.83,"width":1080.86,"height":456.83},"name":"Google Shape;128;p20","placeholder":"body","text":"Angular standalone organiza las vistas; servicios separan física, estado, animación y gráficas.\nCanvas + requestAnimationFrame anima el perfil y las partículas.\nChart.js presenta y(x), y(t), v(T), v(μ) y f(n).\nCuatro pruebas unitarias validan fórmulas, armónicos y extremos fijos.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":37.33,"typeface":"Libre Franklin","color":"#143393","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/fu1gfa1s","slideIndex":7,"text":""}
